.TH ASIKAD 1 "2026-05-09" "Asika" "System Commands"
.SH NAME
asikad \- Asika Daemon with merge queue, web dashboard, and bot integrations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asikad
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B asikad
daemon provides the backend for Asika PR management.
It handles merge queue processing, web dashboard, webhook events,
and bot integrations (Telegram, Feishu, Discord, Slack).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-desktop
Run in desktop foreground mode.
Opens browser to WebUI automatically.
.TP
.BI \-version
Print version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ASIKA_CONFIG
Path to configuration file.
Default is
.BI /etc/asika_config.toml .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in TOML format.
See
.B asika.toml.example
for full reference.
.SS Server Configuration
.TP
.B [server]
listen = ":8080"
.br
mode = "release"
.br
enable_web_update = true
.SS Database
.TP
.B [database]
path = "/var/lib/asika/asika.db"
.SS Authentication
.TP
.B [auth]
jwt_secret = "secret"
.br
token_expiry = "72h"
.SS Platform Tokens
.TP
.B [tokens]
github = "ghp_xxx"
.br
gitlab = "glpat-xxx"
.br
gitea = "gitea_xxx"
.SS Events
.TP
.B [events]
mode = "webhook"
.br
webhook_secret = "secret"
.br
polling_interval = "5m"
.SS Merge Queue
.TP
.B [[repo_groups]]
name = "my-project"
.br
mode = "single"
.br
github = "owner/repo"
.SS Spam Detection
.TP
.B [spam]
enabled = true
.br
threshold = 3
.SS Stale PR Management
.TP
.B [stale]
enabled = true
.br
days_until_stale = 21
.SS Bot Integrations
.TP
.B [telegram]
enabled = true
.br
token = "bot-token"
.br
admin_ids = [12345678]
.br
operator_ids = [11111111]
.br
viewer_ids = [22222222]
.TP
.B [feishu]
enabled = true
.br
app_id = "cli_xxx"
.br
admin_ids = ["ou_xxx"]
.br
operator_ids = ["ou_yyy"]
.TP
.B [discord]
enabled = true
.br
token = "discord-token"
.br
admin_ids = ["user_id_1"]
.br
operator_ids = ["user_id_2"]
.TP
.B [slack]
enabled = true
.br
token = "xoxb-token"
.br
admin_ids = ["U0123456789"]
.br
operator_ids = ["U0987654321"]
.SH API ENDPOINTS
.SS Authentication
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/auth/login
Login with username/password. Returns JWT token.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/auth/logout
Logout (blacklists JWT token).
.SS PR Management
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/repos/:group/prs
List PRs (filters: state, platform, is_draft, author, label).
Requires: viewer+ role, repo group access.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id
Get PR details.
Requires: viewer+ role, repo group access.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/approve
Approve PR.
Requires: approve permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/close
Close PR.
Requires: close permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/reopen
Reopen PR.
Requires: reopen permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/spam
Mark as spam.
Requires: spam permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/comment
Comment on PR.
Requires: viewer+ role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/rebase
Rebase PR onto base branch.
Requires: merge permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/:id/cherry-pick
Cherry-pick merged PR.
Requires: merge permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/batch/approve
Batch approve PRs.
Requires: approve permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/batch/close
Batch close PRs.
Requires: close permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/repos/:group/prs/batch/label
Batch label PRs.
Requires: viewer+ role.
.SS Queue Management
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/queue/:group
Get merge queue.
Requires: viewer+ role, repo group access.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/queue/:group/recheck
Trigger queue recheck.
Requires: manage_queue permission.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/queue/:group/rebase
Rebase all queue items.
Requires: manage_queue permission.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/queue/:group
Clear all queue items.
Requires: manage_queue permission.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/queue/:group/:id
Remove specific PR from queue.
Requires: manage_queue permission.
.SS User Management
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/users
List all users.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/users
Create user.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B PUT /api/v1/users/:username
Update user.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/users/:username
Delete user.
Requires: admin role.
.SS API Key Management
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/apikeys
Create API key. Returns key with raw secret (shown once).
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/apikeys
List all API keys (raw secrets not shown).
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B DELETE /api/v1/apikeys/:id
Revoke API key.
Requires: admin role.
.SS Stats & Usage
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/stats
Get DORA metrics and overview statistics.
Requires: any authenticated user.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/usage
Get real-time CPU and memory usage.
Requires: any authenticated user.
.SS Audit Logs
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/logs
Get audit logs (?level=info|warn|error, ?export=csv).
Requires: viewer+ role.
.SS Sync History
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/sync/history
Get sync history.
Requires: viewer+ role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/sync/retry/:id
Retry failed sync.
Requires: viewer+ role.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/config
Get current config (admin only, secrets masked).
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B PUT /api/v1/config
Update config (admin only, hot-reloadable).
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/config/history
Get config version history.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/config/rollback
Rollback config to a previous version.
Requires: admin role.
.SS Admin Operations
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/admin/backup
Create database backup.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/admin/backups
List available backups.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/admin/restore
Restore from backup.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/test/notify
Send test notification.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/stale/check
Trigger stale PR check.
Requires: admin role.
.SS Self-Update
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/self-update/check
Check for new version.
Requires: admin role.
.TP
.B GET /api/v1/self-update/run
Perform self-update (SSE progress).
Requires: admin role.
.SS Webhooks
.TP
.B POST /webhook/:group/:platform
Receive platform webhooks (GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Forgejo, Codeberg, Bitbucket).
HMAC signature verified.
.TP
.B POST /api/v1/feishu/event
Feishu event callback.
.SS Health Check
.TP
.B GET /health
Health check endpoint (no auth required).
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Two authentication methods are supported:
.TP
.B JWT (Bearer token)
Obtained via
.B POST /api/v1/auth/login
with username/password. Token is passed via
.B Authorization: Bearer <token>
header or
.B asika
_token cookie. Default expiry: 72h.
.TP
.B API Key
Long-lived key for CI/CD and external integrations. Created via
.B POST /api/v1/apikeys
(admin only). Passed via
.B X-API-Key: <key>
header. Format: ak_<64 hex chars>. Stored as bcrypt hash.
.SH PERMISSION MODEL
Three-tier role hierarchy with six granular permissions:
.TS
center box;
cb cb cb cb
l c c c.
Role	Admin	Operator	Viewer
_
View PRs	✅	✅	✅
Approve PRs	✅	Configurable	❌
Merge/Rebase	✅	Configurable	❌
Close PRs	✅	Configurable	❌
Reopen PRs	✅	Configurable	❌
Mark Spam	✅	Configurable	❌
Manage Queue	✅	Configurable	❌
User Management	✅	❌	❌
Config Management	✅	❌	❌
API Key Management	✅	❌	❌
.TE
Admins bypass all permission and repo group checks.
.SH WEB DASHBOARD
The web dashboard is available at the server address (default: http://localhost:8080).
.TP
.B /wizard
First-time setup wizard.
.TP
.B /login
User login page.
.TP
.B /dashboard
Main dashboard with DORA metrics, overview stats, PR breakdowns, recent activity.
.TP
.B /prs
PR list view with filtering.
.TP
.B /repos/:group/prs/:id
Individual PR detail view.
.TP
.B /queue
Merge queue management.
.TP
.B /users
User management (admin).
.TP
.B /apikeys
API key management (admin) — create, list, revoke keys.
.TP
.B /usage
Real-time system usage (CPU, memory, GOMEMLIMIT).
.TP
.B /settings
Merge queue config, spam detection, stale PR management, label rules, config history.
.TP
.B /config
Raw TOML editor, system info, self-update (admin).
.SH BOT COMMANDS
All four bot platforms (Telegram, Feishu, Discord, Slack) support the same command structure:
.TP
.B User Management (admin only)
adduser <username> <password> <role> [groups]
.br
deluser <username>
.br
listusers
.TP
.B API Key Management (admin only)
apikey new <name> <role>
.br
apikey list
.br
apikey revoke <key_id>
.TP
.B PR Operations
prs [group] — List PRs
.br
pr <group> <id> — Show PR details
.br
approve <group> <id> — Approve PR
.br
close <group> <id> — Close PR
.br
reopen <group> <id> — Reopen PR
.br
spam <group> <id> — Mark as spam
.TP
.B Queue Operations
queue [group] — Show merge queue
.br
recheck — Trigger queue recheck
.br
queue_clear — Clear queue
.TP
.B System
stats — DORA metrics
.br
usage — CPU/memory usage
.br
config — Show config summary
.br
version — Show version info
.br
help — Show all commands
.SH INSTALLATION
Install the binary and setup systemd service:
.TP
Copy binary:
.B cp asikad /usr/local/bin/
.TP
Install service:
.B cp pack/debian/asikad.service /etc/systemd/system/
.TP
Enable and start:
.B systemctl enable asikad && systemctl start asikad
.SH FILES
.I /etc/asika_config.toml
Main configuration file.
.I /var/lib/asika/asika.db
Default database path.
.I /var/log/asikad.log
Log file (if configured).
